\TableCaption{holdout-history-early}{The first three enrollment waves. Each row has 500 treatment and 500 control prospects, \$11,000 treatment spending and zero control focal spending. T / C lists buyers through all routes.}
\VAR{b_history_early}
\Section{Credited and incremental cost}
With equal arm sizes, additional buyers are treatment buyers minus control buyers. Credited CAC divides \$11,000 by all treatment buyers. iCAC divides the same amount by additional buyers. For unequal arms, the scaling in Appendix A1 applies to both control acquisitions and costs.
\Section{Separate comparisons for each wave}
The source preserves separate test identifiers, assignment dates and end dates. A prospect is never reused in another test. The monthly estimates are not pooled: an old conversion rate cannot substitute for the current wave's background acquisition rate.
\Evidence{Saved SQL: \Code{channel_cac.csv}. The original July arm records are preserved; subsequent waves extend the acquisition-only history.}

