\PageTitle{C1 / SEGMENTATION DIAGNOSTICS}{The explanatory value\newline of baseline customer groups}{Same customers, six-payment contribution and two groups per candidate strategy.}
\Section{Within-cell homogeneity and across-cell heterogeneity}
With the population and outcome fixed, reducing weighted within-cell variance increases between-cell variance:
\[
\operatorname{Var}(Y)=\sum_g w_g\operatorname{Var}(Y\mid g)
+\sum_g w_g(\bar Y_g-\bar Y)^2,\qquad w_g=n_g/N.
\]
Population variances use the group-size divisor. The course grouping exercise demonstrates this objective while holding customer values and cell count fixed (\SourceCite{course2026}{Tian, 2026}, Topic 1, slides 37--39).
