The recorded Python environment is installed with \Code{uv sync --frozen}; commands run through \Code{uv run --frozen}. The model uses CPU JAX/NumPyro; a GPU is not required. The analysis begins with the released records and does not regenerate them. Source hashes, saved SQL, model settings, figure data and document assets remain bound to the output manifests.
\Boundary{Alternative models must use the same information available at the observation cutoff. Later outcomes are reserved for prospective evaluation and cannot inform features, parameter tuning or revisions to the input snapshot. Human review remains a gate between analytical stages.}

\NewPage
\PageTitle{E7 / THE SKILL-DRIVEN WORKFLOW}{How the skill drives\newline analysis and report generation}{Instructions, executable work and verification have distinct roles in one reproducible process.}
\Section{The skills define the work}
The root \Code{SKILL.md} sets the business question, data boundaries, analytical stages and review gates. The optional student-teacher skill presents intermediate evidence at nineteen learner-controlled checkpoints, with the report last. The executive-report skill specifies the audience, narrative, evidence requirements and visual checks. The Version B contract places findings and decisions in the fifteen-page main report, with full methods and source detail here in the appendix.

The skills guide execution and judgment; they do not calculate the results. They direct the analyst to the versioned code, configuration, source assets and acceptance checks needed to produce the deliverable.

\Section{The code and configuration execute the analysis}
Canonical SQL transforms the separate exports into cohort and company views. Model settings define the renewal, revenue and valuation calculations. Saved outputs feed the charts, narrative quantities, tables and TeX templates. Human judgments are recorded separately from computed evidence.

The frozen 1.7.0 report and the original B comparison remain preserved. This B revision uses dataset 5.1: the seven operational CSVs and fitted models are unchanged, while five monthly waves extend the original July acquisition tests. Current cost selection and the contribution-path comparison are rebuilt from saved tables. Reused model-input hashes must match the freshly rebuilt operating inputs.

\Section{The manifests and checks establish reproduction}
Source hashes, SQL, model settings, output tables, figure data, template/style files and the skills are bound into manifests. A report replay verifies the frozen fitted outputs and rebuilds the observed analysis, diagrams and document in a fresh directory. Two separate replay processes are compared before claiming same-environment reproduction.

Install the locked Python environment with \Code{uv sync --frozen}; run project commands through \Code{uv run --frozen}. The accompanying \Code{docs/report-version-b.md} gives the complete B build and comparison commands. The public workflow needs the repository's bundled skills, not a private skill installation.

\Section{Review is part of the handoff}
Numerical integrity, compilation and visual inspection are separate checks. The report retains editable TeX, figure assets, the exhibit registry and its source map. The source map on the next page connects the executive exhibits to the saved evidence.

